{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_15","type":"agent_message","text":"**NOT READY.** The revised probe could still pass if all three v12 answers state the 85.4% estimate without citing a source. That would be marked unsupported, but the outcome rule only blocks omission or a counted wrong attribution. [Part B reading and outcome](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-21-citation-lists/PROBE-DESIGN.md:75)\n\n1. **Fix the Part B targets and pass rule.** For `old-2:6955`, the saved retry `6979` cites and pushes `e3768`, the SEC filing that explicitly says NVIDIA entered a definitive agreement on September 2. The target omits it and lists `e3965`, whose quote only says NVIDIA agreed to acquire Hugging Face. Freeze which sources support the exact claim and distinguish multiple valid sources from genuinely unclear intent. Count wrong attribution by the claim the source is used for, even if the source supports a different claim in the same answer. An unsupported material fact in all three draws should receive the same outcome as a material omission. [Frozen targets](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-21-citation-lists/probe-targets.json:16) · [Pass rule](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-21-citation-lists/PROBE-DESIGN.md:106)\n\n2. **Make Part C compare what the answers say and what their sources support.** `control-1:8790` gives Bloomberg’s $393B estimate as the reference and about $390B as the judge’s own forecast. All three v12 answers could keep the same citations and forecast range while claiming Bloomberg supplied the $390B forecast. The current reading packet would surface neither a changed source nor an out-of-range answer. Read changed references, forecasts and uses of shared sources. Define whether a refused v7 control leaves the comparison incomplete. [Part C reading rule](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-21-citation-lists/PROBE-DESIGN.md:92) · [Reading packets](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-21-citation-lists/PROBE-DESIGN.md:133)\n\n3. **Correct the budget claim and rehearse the actual stops.** I reproduced all 12 starts at saved costs, with **$0.34695** projected core spend and **$0.03734** minimum start margin. At 130% of saved costs, **only 10 start** in the frozen order. The 11th needs $0.13624 in reservations with $0.10672 left. The $0.45103 figure is the projected total if all 12 could run. The start rule covers six first attempts. Retries reserve again, so explicitly allow an admitted comparison to stop incomplete. In the $0 rehearsal, prove that only one Part C comparison can start at a time, that a retry can exhaust the remaining headroom, and that either a blocked start or an interrupted comparison yields **inconclusive**. Also feed three unsupported 85.4% answers through the outcome rule. A marker flag alone does not prove they block a pass. [Start rule](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-21-citation-lists/PROBE-DESIGN.md:49) · [Budget transport](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/e2e-comparison-2026-11-13/budget_replay.py:268) · [Rehearsal](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-21-citation-lists/PROBE-DESIGN.md:136)"}}
